Awesome GPT Image 2.5 Prompts is open source.

The scripts are MIT. Everything we wrote around them -- the collection itself,
the nine use cases, the ordering, the prose, the translations -- is CC BY 4.0.
Fork it, build on it, ship it commercially. Credit us and you are done.

    Copyright (c) 2026 Formative Intelligence Inc.

    scripts/**                     MIT           LICENSES/MIT.txt
    everything else we wrote       CC BY 4.0     LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

The prompts are a different matter, and it is the one thing worth reading
carefully. We collected them; we did not write them. Each one belongs to the
person credited on its row, who published it publicly, and ATTRIBUTION.md
records who that is and where they posted it. 115 reached us through a
collection that stated CC0 1.0 and 35 through one that stated CC BY 4.0; both
statements are recorded per row, and copies of what each collection said are in
provenance/.

So: the collection is ours to give you, and the prompts are theirs. If you want
to build on a prompt for something that matters, the credit line tells you
whose it is. If you wrote one and want it gone, TAKEDOWN.md -- it goes, no
explanation needed.

GitHub reads this file, finds no single SPDX identifier, and labels the
repository "Other". REUSE.toml has the machine-readable map.
